These are accounting and origin invariants over real observations, not a
second expression computing the model's expected result. Callbacks are never
re-evaluated by the specification. Divergence is permitted.
Julia source: base/intfuncs.jl:308-341 at
f755f49a9e41380d7da126b3c1db9fe7f83dd027.
Documented purpose/errors: base/intfuncs.jl:289-306. -/
def InvmodOpenDispatchProvenance : Prop :=
  ∀ (W V Ty P State Other : Type) (ops : InvmodOps W V Ty P State Other)
      (n m : V) (world : W),
    match invmodInteger (observeInvmodOps ops) n m (world, []) with
    | none => True
    | some (.ok (value, (final, trace))) =>
        (∀ before event after, trace = before ++ event :: after → InvmodEventCausal n m before event) ∧
        InvmodCallAccounting trace ∧ InvmodWorldAccounting world final trace ∧ InvmodTerminal m trace (.ok value)
    | some (.error (error, (final, trace))) =>
        (∀ before event after, trace = before ++ event :: after → InvmodEventCausal n m before event) ∧
